# {{project_name}}

Generated by the `automation-generation` skill (binding `playwright-ts`) from the
approved test cases with `Needs Automation = TRUE`. See `../AutomationGeneration.md`
for the case mapping, locators and validation.

## Prerequisites and first-run setup

- Node.js 18+, npm; network access to {{base_url}}
- `npm ci` (or `npm install`), then `npx playwright install chromium` — the browser build
  must match the pinned Playwright {{playwright_version}}

## Environment variables

| Name | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `{{username_env_var}}` | yes | Login user name — never stored in the project |
| `{{password_env_var}}` | yes | Login password — never stored in the project |
| `QA_BASE_URL` | no | Entry point (default `{{base_url}}`) |
| `QA_BROWSER` | no | `chromium` (default), `firefox`, `webkit` |
| `QA_HEADLESS` | no | `true` (default) / `false` |
| `QA_TIMEOUT_MS` | no | Action / assertion / wait timeout (default {{default_timeout_ms}}) |
| `QA_ARTIFACTS_DIR` | no | Evidence root (default `{{default_artifacts_dir}}`) |
| `QA_RUN_ID` | no | Run identifier used in evidence paths |

## Run from the command line (Claude Code)

```
# PowerShell: $env:{{username_env_var}} = "<value>"; $env:{{password_env_var}} = "<value>"
npx playwright test
```

`npm run typecheck` (tsc), `npm run list` (discovery only, writes no reports).

## Run from IntelliJ IDEA (Community)

Open the folder; Run > Edit Configurations > **{{run_name}}** (Shell Script, shared in `.run/`):
fill the two credential variables locally; run.

## Results

`<QA_ARTIFACTS_DIR>/<run-id>/{{binding_dir}}/`: `html-report/`, `results.json`, `junit.xml`,
and `<case-id>/` with `steps.log`, `final.png` (pass) or `failure.png` + `trace.zip` (fail).
Steps that type secrets run before tracing starts. Retries are 0.
